// Waives a Verilator UNOPTFLAT false positive on hydrogen's bus_D, only
// reproducible once the real core_glue and the real bram are wired
// together (core_glue's own isolated testbench drives bus_D.rdata
// directly, so the cycle never forms there). core_glue's combinational
// address/data-in-one-block (bus_D.addr computed from `instruction`;
// write.value read from bus_D.rdata, both inside the same always_comb)
// is a real, one-directional, feed-forward dependency: instruction ->
// bus_D.addr -> (bram) -> bus_D.rdata -> write.value. Verilator's
// per-block (not per-signal) UNOPTFLAT analysis can't always prove that
// isn't circular when both sides of a combinational-read memory bus are
// touched in one procedural block -- see
// https://verilator.org/warn/UNOPTFLAT. Scoped to bus_if.sv so it only
// silences this specific interface's instances, not lint generally; only
// pulled in by hydrogen.core, so it doesn't mask a real UNOPTFLAT
// elsewhere.
`verilator_config
lint_off -rule UNOPTFLAT -file "*/bus_if.sv" -match "*bus_D*"
